# Line endings.
#
# Everything text gets stored in the repository as LF and checked out as LF, on
# every platform. Without this, git relies on each person's core.autocrlf, so
# the same file can come out CRLF on one machine and LF on another and show up
# as a whole-file diff that has nothing to do with the change.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch files are the exception, since cmd.exe is happier with CRLF.
# kam_host.bat is generated per install and gitignored, but if a committed .bat
# ever appears it should still get the right endings.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary files, marked explicitly so git never tries to normalise them. It
# detects most of these anyway, but a mistake here corrupts the file rather
# than just producing a noisy diff, so it's worth being clear.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.ico  binary
*.wav  binary
*.pt   binary
*.db   binary
*.zip  binary
